{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 8514425228183210935, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 699, "mtime": 1791871737.0084171, "sha256": "84c5a48e62e6f7704759d6031a89088215d82794cf6dbe7fb0003a3bf5890e2b"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 507, "mtime": 1791871741.0367463, "sha256": "1f39795a0b8e5fbc019c4118b9968b01dc24249ce2c9f2d711b747ba150f2d0c"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/8/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/8/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running the suite.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Why it happened:** a float can't store 2.675 exactly; the value actually kept is 2.67499999999999982\u2026. Python's built-in `round()` works on that stored value (and rounds exact halves to the even digit), so it went down to 2.67.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the number back into its shortest decimal form (\"2.675\") and rounds that half up to the cent with Python's `decimal` module. It still returns a float, so callers like `add_vat` don't need to change.\n\n**Test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, which checks 2.675, 1.005, 0.125, 2.674, -2.675, 3 and `add_vat(10.0)`. pytest isn't installed here, so I couldn't run the files through it. I ran the same cases directly in Python instead: all passed, and the existing `test_split` still passes.\n\nTwo behaviours to know about:\n- Negative halves round away from zero, so `-2.675` becomes `-2.68`.\n- If a calculation lands just below a half before rounding (for example a multiplication that gives 1.00499999\u2026 when you meant 1.005), it still rounds down. Only switching prices to `Decimal` throughout would avoid that, and I didn't make that change.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 246155, "requests_cache_write": 14688, "requests_cost_usd": 0.175191, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2622, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial8", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 14, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:08:40.997973+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls